kenning (0.7.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Removed the optional photos of failed attempts, which could photograph
    people who never agreed to it; photos already saved are deleted on upgrade

 -- Rishon Jonathan R <mithicalaviator85@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 14:33:41 +0530

kenning (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Works in dim rooms: dark infrared frames that show a face are used, about
    a third faster
  * Separate too dark and too bright messages; the lock screen keeps the
    failure reason visible
  * Photos of failed attempts (off by default) and Try Face Again on the
    login screen
  * Gentler Set Up tilts, with tilting up optional, and reasons for skipped
    steps
  * Security fixes: SSH requests outside a local session, theme archive
    limits, a lockout that survives restarts

 -- Rishon Jonathan R <mithicalaviator85@gmail.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 01:54:21 +0530

kenning (0.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Guided face setup: look straight, then turn left, right, up and down, with
    a confirmation and countdown first, and the steps read aloud. An animated
    head shows each turn, and you look back at the camera between turns.
  * Set Up previews the ordinary webcam instead of the infrared picture.
  * The settings page is laid out like Plasma's own, with pages for faces,
    animation, and recognition and security.
  * Default look names from the account's display name.
  * A "Try Face Again" button on the lock screen after face unlock fails.
  * Frames washed out by bright light are skipped like dark ones.

 -- Rishon Jonathan R <mithicalaviator85@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:42:35 +0530

